reviews.body:
That did it, thanks @pcbeingused333! The fallback template renders again, and `mediaFolder` now loads for both sides of the `??`.

One more spot I ran into, not blocking: a `for` over a filtered or conditional sequence still glues the paths. After the same fallback set, `{% for t in media.thumbnails|slice(0, 1) %}{{ t.url }}{% endfor %}` adds `cover.media.thumbnails.media.thumbnails`. Resolving the sequence like a set value fixed it when I tried it, and it would also replace the new special branch:

```php
if ($node instanceof ForNode) {
    $source = $node->getNode('value_target')->getAttribute('name');
    $targets = $this->getVariables([$node->getNode('seq')], $aliases);

    $aliases[$source] = \count($targets) <= 1 ? (string) (reset($targets) ?: '') : array_values($targets);
}
```

Fine with it as is too, so approving.

